# SKINIC Project Conventions

Read `SKINIC-ecosystem/HANDOFF.md` for full context before starting any task.

## Repo Map

| Folder | Purpose | Deploy |
|---|---|---|
| `SKINIC/` | FastAPI backend — `main.py` is the single entry point | Railway → `api.skinic.app` |
| `skinic-web/` | Next.js — landing page + user dashboard | Vercel → `skinic.app` |
| `skinic-mobile/` | React Native Expo — consumer app | EAS → App Store/Play Store |

## AI Branding — Critical

- ❌ NEVER mention "DeepSeek", "HuggingFace model IDs", or any underlying AI provider in public UI, API responses, docs, or logs
- ✅ Always use "SKINIC AI", "SKINIC Skin Intelligence Engine", "SKINIC Clinical Guard"

## Backend (`SKINIC/main.py`)

- Single file — all routes, middleware, helpers are in `main.py`
- JWT verification is LOCAL (cached JWKS) — do not add outbound HTTP calls per request
- Tier limits live in `TIER_LIMITS` dict — this is the source of truth
- API key format: `sk-` + `secrets.token_urlsafe(32)`
- Key stored as SHA-256 hash — never store raw keys in DB

## Frontend (`skinic-web/`)

- Dashboard server pages MUST have:
  ```typescript
  export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
  export const revalidate = 0;
  ```
- Use `createAdminClient()` for server-side Supabase queries (bypasses RLS)
- Use `createClient()` for client-side Supabase (anon key)
- Dashboard client components call backend `/dashboard/*` with `Authorization: Bearer <jwt>`

## Deployment

- Backend: push to `main` → Railway auto-deploys
- Frontend: push to `main` → Vercel auto-deploys
- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, `venv/`, `node_modules/`

## Supabase

- Project ref: `jwenabxcecncybnmeybr`
- `SUPABASE_URL` must NOT have trailing `/rest/v1/`
- RLS is enabled — always use service role key for server-side admin queries
